WEBVTT


00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:06.570
Here's a beautiful, soft trim that
can be used as a hem or a band.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:13.440
It's easy and it can be worked at any
gauge on any machine with any stitch

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.040
pattern.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.820
Adding a unique touch
to your next project.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.830
It also lays fairly flat
right off the machine.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.950
Taming that dreaded stockinette curl.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.555
It's a good option to replace ribbing.

00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:39.525
Get started by casting on with waste yarn
and Ravel cord to make it even faster.

00:00:39.555 --> 00:00:43.245
You might consider using a
cast on rag and Ravel cord.

00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:49.515
We're going to be forming a small
hem, so this step is not optional.

00:00:52.055 --> 00:00:56.165
Knit five rows, hang
your cast on stitches.

00:00:56.565 --> 00:01:00.225
And knit one row at one
number looser tension.

00:01:12.795 --> 00:01:14.925
Change back to your band tension.

00:01:17.645 --> 00:01:19.295
Set your machine to hold.

00:01:20.315 --> 00:01:22.475
Pull out every nine needles.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.100
I'm using the Knit it Now cheat sheets to
select my needles so I don't have to count

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.330
all the way across the bed.

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:32.660
Why nine needles?

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.810
Well, do your own thing
here in this photo.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:40.310
The scallops line up with the stitch
pattern, so figure out how many needles

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.830
and how wide your
scallops are going to be.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.790
While holding these stitches.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.890
Slowly knit a few rows.

00:01:51.085 --> 00:01:55.824
As you knit, you'll see the loops
building up on the held needles.

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:58.615
This is forming the scallops.

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:05.304
Watch the hooks on either side of those
held needles and make sure the stitches

00:02:05.304 --> 00:02:06.655
don't pop off.

00:02:08.354 --> 00:02:11.505
Putting a little weight
on each scallop helps.

00:02:11.985 --> 00:02:17.805
You might want to pull the needles on each
side of those held needles out a bit to

00:02:17.805 --> 00:02:19.095
make the knitting easier.

00:02:21.555 --> 00:02:23.325
Use your judgment here.

00:02:23.415 --> 00:02:29.505
The pattern says to knit eight rows with
this thick yarn, I'm using, eight rows

00:02:29.505 --> 00:02:30.435
were just too many.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:40.820
When you're ready to finish the scallop,
turn off the hold setting and slowly,

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:46.399
carefully knit across all the stitches
and confirm that everything knit properly.

00:02:48.109 --> 00:02:53.959
Remove any excess weight, switch to your
stitch pattern if you're using one and

00:02:53.959 --> 00:03:00.010
continue knitting your garment
to use this technique as a band,

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.980
knit across all the stitches
to form the scallops

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:08.280
knit.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.690
One more row.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:15.420
I like to do this to be safe and remove
the work on waste yarn or a garter bar.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:22.170
Hang your garment in the needles, pushing
the work back all the way past those

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.010
needle latches.

00:03:26.695 --> 00:03:30.685
Then hang the stitches of your
band in the hooks of the needles.

00:03:40.045 --> 00:03:45.655
Close the latches and pull the stitches
through the garment pickup edge.

00:03:55.685 --> 00:03:58.325
Just bind off with the
method of your choice.

00:03:58.985 --> 00:04:01.685
I like to use a back stitch bind off.

00:04:02.225 --> 00:04:06.665
It's neat and tidy and almost
impossible to work too tightly.

00:04:08.795 --> 00:04:13.865
Add some in the in-the-ditch button holes
and you've got a really pretty finish.

00:04:14.325 --> 00:04:15.525
For your new cardigan.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.985
Thank you for watching.

00:04:21.915 --> 00:04:26.355
Look for other buttonhole and band
techniques in the learning library.

00:04:26.985 --> 00:04:32.865
Subscribers have full access to hundreds
of tutorials on a wide variety of topics

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:34.485
and all skill levels.

00:04:35.265 --> 00:04:37.485
Please consider becoming a subscriber.

00:04:38.205 --> 00:04:39.275
Happy knitting.

